.TITLE "find"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Searches for files in a directory hierarchy. It finds files based on __attributes__ like name, type, size, and modification time.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**find . -name "pattern"**
Searches for files with a specific name or pattern in the current directory.
> __.__ search path | __-name__ name flag | __"pattern"__ search term

**find . -type f**
Filters the search to only include regular files.
> __-type__ type flag | __f__ file type

**find . -type d**
Filters the search to only include directories.
> __-type__ type flag | __d__ directory type

**find . -mtime -7**
Finds files that were modified within the last seven days.
> __-mtime__ modification time flag | __-7__ number of days

**find . -size +100M**
Locates files that are larger than 100 megabytes.
> __-size__ size flag | __+100M__ size threshold

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __find__ command is extremely powerful when combined with the __-exec__ flag to perform actions on discovered files. Always test your search patterns first without destructive actions to ensure accuracy.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:mdfind** **mac:grep**

